*— Ends —*';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-007-001', 'SAFETY_DOC_007', 1, 'preamble — header and disclaimer', '# HEALTHONE GROUP — MEDICATION SAFETY COMMUNICATION

**Document ID:** SAFETY_DOC_007
**Issued:** 1 March 2026
**Classification:** Safety Communication — Action Required

> **SYNTHETIC DOCUMENT — NOT REAL MEDICAL GUIDANCE.** This document is
> fabricated for the purposes of a software demonstration. CardioZen is an
> invented medication that does not exist. Nothing in this document describes
> any real product, and nothing in it should be used to inform any clinical
> decision.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-007-002', 'SAFETY_DOC_007', 2, 'section 1 — Purpose', '## 1. Purpose

This communication informs prescribers, pharmacists and clinical review staff
of a monitoring requirement applying to patients treated with CardioZen who
also carry a diagnosis of chronic kidney disease. It supersedes no previous
communication. It takes effect on the date of issue.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-007-003', 'SAFETY_DOC_007', 3, 'section 2 — Background', '## 2. Background

CardioZen is cleared substantially by renal excretion. In patients whose
kidney function is already reduced, clearance is slower and plasma
concentrations accumulate over a period of weeks. The principal consequence of
accumulation is a rise in serum potassium.

Post-marketing surveillance across the HealthOne network identified eleven
cases over the preceding eighteen months in which potassium elevation was
identified only after the patient became symptomatic. In nine of those eleven
cases, no potassium measurement had been recorded in the preceding six months.
The Committee''s view is that the interval between measurements, rather than
the availability of the measurement itself, was the contributing factor.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-007-004', 'SAFETY_DOC_007', 4, 'section 3 — Monitoring requirement', '## 3. Monitoring requirement

For any patient receiving CardioZen who has a recorded diagnosis of chronic
kidney disease, serum potassium should be checked at least every three months
for the duration of therapy.

The requirement applies from the date of this communication. It applies to
patients already established on CardioZen as well as to new starts. Where a
patient has had no potassium measurement within the stated interval, the
responsible clinical team should arrange one.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-007-005', 'SAFETY_DOC_007', 5, 'section 4 — Population not covered by this requirement', '## 4. Population not covered by this requirement

Patients receiving CardioZen who do not carry a diagnosis of chronic kidney
disease are outside the scope of section 3. The Committee considered whether to
extend the requirement to all CardioZen recipients and concluded that the
evidence does not presently support it.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-007-006', 'SAFETY_DOC_007', 6, 'section 5 — Reporting', '## 5. Reporting

Suspected adverse reactions should be reported through the usual HealthOne
pharmacovigilance channel. Reporting is not a substitute for the monitoring
described in section 3.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-007-007', 'SAFETY_DOC_007', 7, 'section 6 — Review', '## 6. Review

This communication will be reviewed within twelve months of issue, or earlier
if surveillance data warrant it.

*— End of document —*';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-008-001', 'SAFETY_DOC_008', 1, 'preamble — header and disclaimer', '# MEMORANDUM

**To:** Prescribing leads; renal services; clinical review team
**From:** Chair, Medication Safety Committee
**Memo reference:** SAFETY_DOC_008
**Date:** 15 August 2026
**Subject:** Shortening of the potassium monitoring interval — CardioZen with
chronic kidney disease

> **SYNTHETIC DOCUMENT — NOT REAL MEDICAL GUIDANCE.** Fabricated for a
> software demonstration. CardioZen is an invented medication. Nothing here
> describes a real product or should inform any clinical decision.
>
> **HELD BACK FROM THE SYSTEM.** This document is deliberately not loaded
> during normal operation. It is introduced live to demonstrate the path from
> a new document to a governed, active monitoring rule. See
> docs/self-tracking/03_SCHEMA_DESIGN.md §13.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-008-002', 'SAFETY_DOC_008', 2, 'section 1 — Why we are revising', '## 1. Why we are revising

In March of this year the Committee issued SAFETY_DOC_007, which required
serum potassium to be checked at least every three months for patients
receiving CardioZen with a diagnosis of chronic kidney disease. Five months of
operating experience is now available.

Two findings prompt this revision. First, among patients who did develop
clinically significant potassium elevation while compliant with the
three-month interval, the elevation was in most cases detectable earlier than
the next scheduled measurement would have caught it. Second, the interval
performed least well in precisely the group at highest risk — those with the
most reduced renal function — because in that group accumulation proceeds
faster than the interval assumes.

The Committee''s judgement is that the interval published in March is too long
for this population.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-008-003', 'SAFETY_DOC_008', 3, 'section 2 — Revised requirement', '## 2. Revised requirement

For patients receiving CardioZen who have a recorded diagnosis of chronic
kidney disease, serum potassium must be checked every 60 days for the duration
of therapy.

This replaces the three-month interval published in SAFETY_DOC_007 section 3.
It takes effect on the date of this memorandum.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-008-004', 'SAFETY_DOC_008', 4, 'section 3 — What this means in practice', '## 3. What this means in practice

Patients whose most recent potassium measurement falls within the new interval
require no immediate action; they move onto the shorter schedule from their
next measurement. Patients whose most recent measurement is older than the new
interval should have one arranged.

The Committee wishes to be explicit on one point: this revision is not a
statement that previously compliant care was substandard. It is a change to a
threshold in light of new operating data, and it should be communicated to
patients in those terms if the question arises.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-008-005', 'SAFETY_DOC_008', 5, 'section 4 — Scope unchanged', '## 4. Scope unchanged

The population remains as defined in SAFETY_DOC_007 — CardioZen recipients
with a diagnosis of chronic kidney disease. This memorandum makes no change
for patients without that diagnosis, and introduces no requirement for any
test other than serum potassium.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-008-006', 'SAFETY_DOC_008', 6, 'section 5 — Status of SAFETY_DOC_007', '## 5. Status of SAFETY_DOC_007

SAFETY_DOC_007 should be treated as superseded in respect of the monitoring
interval in its section 3. Its remaining sections stand.

*— Ends —*';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-009-001', 'SAFETY_DOC_009', 1, 'preamble — header and disclaimer', '# PHARMACOVIGILANCE ADVISORY

**Advisory:** SAFETY_DOC_009
**Issued:** 10 April 2026
**Unit:** Pharmacovigilance
**Action:** Awareness. No change to monitoring practice.

> **SYNTHETIC DOCUMENT — NOT REAL MEDICAL GUIDANCE.** Fabricated for a
> software demonstration. CardioZen is an invented medication. Nothing here
> describes a real product or should inform any clinical decision.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-009-002', 'SAFETY_DOC_009', 2, 'section 1 — Summary of the signal', '## 1. Summary of the signal

Between October 2025 and March 2026 the Unit received thirty-one reports of
dizziness in patients receiving CardioZen. Reports originated from all three
sites and from two community pharmacy partners. Onset was described as within
the first fortnight of therapy in the majority of reports and as transient in
twenty-four of the thirty-one.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-009-003', 'SAFETY_DOC_009', 3, 'section 2 — Assessment', '## 2. Assessment

The Unit assessed the reports for a dose relationship and did not find one.
Twelve of the thirty-one reports described concurrent initiation of a second
agent with recognised vestibular effects, which the Unit regards as a
plausible alternative explanation in those cases.

Laboratory data were available for nineteen of the reported patients. Serum
potassium was within the reference range in seventeen of the nineteen at the
time closest to symptom onset, and marginally elevated in two. An
electrocardiogram had been recorded in six patients and showed no consistent
abnormality. These figures are presented to characterise the reports; they
describe what happened to be on file and are not a recommendation that either
investigation be performed.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-009-004', 'SAFETY_DOC_009', 4, 'section 3 — Conclusion', '## 3. Conclusion

The Unit''s conclusion is that the reports are consistent with a recognised,
usually self-limiting effect of therapy initiation. **No change to laboratory
monitoring practice arises from this advisory, and no new monitoring interval
is introduced by it.** Existing requirements published elsewhere are unaffected
and continue to apply on their own terms.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-009-005', 'SAFETY_DOC_009', 5, 'section 4 — What clinicians should do', '## 4. What clinicians should do

- Counsel patients starting CardioZen that transient dizziness is recognised
  and usually settles.
- Advise patients to report symptoms that persist beyond two weeks or that
  affect their ability to stand or walk safely.
- Continue to report suspected reactions through the usual channel.';
INSERT INTO DOC_CHUNK (CHUNK_ID, DOC_ID, CHUNK_INDEX, SECTION_LABEL, CHUNK_TEXT)
SELECT 'CHK-009-006', 'SAFETY_DOC_009', 6, 'section 5 — Further work', '## 5. Further work

The Unit will keep the signal under passive surveillance and will re-assess if
the reporting rate changes materially. No routine data collection is being
established for this purpose.

*— End of advisory —*';

